{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788578",
      "title": "Using the output() Function",
      "lectureOrder": 36,
      "videoOrder": 32,
      "sourceHash": "40da358c02bec116583b8b5e83d20db2d2b50ca767b4796ad47386743c29850d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "So you did now learn how to add outputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.533,
          "en": "to your component's custom events, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.52,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "Now using this @Output decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 16.82,
          "en": "is how you would create outputs in most Angular projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.83,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "and is the approach you'll see in most Angular projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 24.603,
          "en": "since this is how you've always created outputs in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "But there actually is a more modern alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "which you might not encounter in that many projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "but which might become more important in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "which is why I also want to introduce you to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "And that alternative does not use this output decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "but instead an output function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 50.613,
          "en": "which you must import from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "Now this output function might look familiar to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "if you recall that input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "which we imported and used earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "to set up Signal-based inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 67.953,
          "en": "so to replace that @Input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "Now we're doing something similar with this output function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "And the idea is that instead of defining a custom event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 79.83,
          "en": "a custom output like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "you still add your property, select in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "but instead of adding @Output in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 92.66,
          "en": "you assign the result of calling the output function to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "This syntax will tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "that select should be an output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "just as the @Output decorator does,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "and that it should under the hood in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "store such an event emitter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 110.13,
          "en": "So you don't need to explicitly create that event emitter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.13,
          "end": 112.92,
          "en": "on your own anymore when using output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.92,
          "end": 114.783,
          "en": "but it's instead done for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 118.02000000000001,
          "en": "Which means that you're still able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.02000000000001,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "and that you still should call emit on this output property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 124.773,
          "en": "so on this select property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 128.31,
          "en": "This still works because under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.31,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "it still stores such an event emitter inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "just one that's automatically created by calling output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "Now one error I do get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "is that the argument of type string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 143.28,
          "en": "so the type of this ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "is not assignable to a parameter of type void,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 148.443,
          "en": "which might look a bit weird.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 151.14,
          "en": "Now this is in the end TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 154.413,
          "en": "complaining about the type of data we're emitting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "We did not get this error when using the other approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "where we created the event emitter ourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "but when using this output function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 167.913,
          "en": "Angular and TypeScript are a bit more strict.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "In the end what we have to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 174.9,
          "en": "is let TypeScript know about the kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.9,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "that will eventually be emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "And we do that by, again, using this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 182.49,
          "en": "strange angle bracket syntax here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.49,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "and between those angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 187.98,
          "en": "we then set the type of value that will be emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.98,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "in this case string, and with that the error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "So by using this generic type feature here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 199.68,
          "en": "by letting TypeScript know about the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.68,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "this output function will operate on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 205.8,
          "en": "so the type of value that will be emitted in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.8,
          "end": 208.11,
          "en": "TypeScript is happy again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.11,
          "end": 210.96,
          "en": "And you can therefore then use this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "this approach here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "instead of setting up the output like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 218.13,
          "en": "Now what's really important to understand is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 223.13,
          "en": "that output is really just a replacement for this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.53,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "it does exactly the same in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 229.89,
          "en": "and therefore you listen to custom events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.89,
          "end": 231.9,
          "en": "created with this output function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.9,
          "end": 236.703,
          "en": "in exactly the same way as if you were using that decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 239.64,
          "en": "So in that app component template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.64,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "we still use event binding like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "to trigger the onSelectUser method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 247.14,
          "en": "whenever that select event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.14,
          "end": 249.57,
          "en": "That works in the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.57,
          "end": 254.07,
          "en": "It's all important to understand that this output function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.07,
          "end": 259.07,
          "en": "does not create any kind of signal or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 263.43,
          "en": "select is in the end still an event emitter thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.43,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "it's not a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 269.7,
          "en": "Unlike the input function which did create an input signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.7,
          "end": 273.21,
          "en": "output doesn't, it still just gives us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.21,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "a custom event we can emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 279.21,
          "en": "Now why does this function exist then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.21,
          "end": 282.753,
          "en": "if it does the same as this code essentially?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.68,
          "end": 288.18,
          "en": "Well, mostly so that if you were using the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.18,
          "end": 292.8,
          "en": "for registering the inputs instead of that input decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.8,
          "end": 294.15,
          "en": "that if you were doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.15,
          "end": 295.98,
          "en": "you could use the output function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 295.98,
          "end": 299.19,
          "en": "so that you don't need any decorators at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 299.19,
          "end": 304.19,
          "en": "neither for inputs nor for outputs inside of that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.65,
          "end": 308.13,
          "en": "besides the component decorator, you still need that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.13,
          "end": 310.14,
          "en": "but no decorators would be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.14,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "inside of that component then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 315.783,
          "en": "That's one reason for the existence of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.65,
          "end": 320.55,
          "en": "In addition, this code of course is shorter than this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.55,
          "end": 323.82,
          "en": "and that's also a good reason to use this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.82,
          "end": 325.233,
          "en": "this syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 331.37,
          "en": "Nonetheless, just as with inputs earlier in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.25,
          "end": 336.84000000000003,
          "en": "in most Angular projects you will see the @Output decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 336.84000000000003,
          "end": 340.68,
          "en": "and this manually created event emitter instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 340.68,
          "end": 344.90999999999997,
          "en": "simply because this approach has been around forever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 344.90999999999997,
          "end": 347.15999999999997,
          "en": "since Angular was released,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 347.15999999999997,
          "end": 351.03,
          "en": "whereas this output function is relatively new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 351.03,
          "end": 353.37,
          "en": "and, hence, you won't encounter it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 353.37,
          "end": 355.92,
          "en": "in that many projects out there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 355.92,
          "end": 359.64,
          "en": "And that's also why I will not use it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 359.64,
          "end": 363.03,
          "en": "why I instead will go back to the @Output decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 363.03,
          "end": 366.69,
          "en": "But of course you should know about this output function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.69,
          "end": 370.383,
          "en": "and you'll also see it again throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
